/*  Failures — `<type> or failure`, `return a failure …`, `or pass the failure off`, `but on failure`,
    `Try to: … In case of failure:`, `the message of the failure`, and reading a file or a folder's
    contents, which can fail.

    ★ A value that may be a failure is `{ ok, value, failure }` — the failure the runtime's own
      `CufetFailure`, a message and a category that is NULL when none was given. Its kind is written
      `failure of <kind>`, `failure of void` for a call made for its effect.

    ★ INSIDE A `Try`, a call that can fail reads as its value: when it fails, the failure is kept and
      the program jumps to the handler — out of the middle of an expression, which gcc allows from a
      statement expression. The emitter's `kinds` map carries the `Try` a statement is in as `%try`,
      so a handler, a function and a block each see the right one.

    ★ `In case of exception` is the runtime's own: a `setjmp` frame on its stack for each `Try` that
      has one, which a fault jumps back to. A jump out of the `Try` any other way — `Return`, `Stop`,
      `Skip`, a failure to a `Try` further out, a failure passed off — closes the frames it leaves, or
      a later fault would jump into a frame that is gone. The `kinds` map counts them: `%exc` open
      here, `%try-exc` and `%loop-exc` open where the failure's `Try` and the loop began.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    Bind fact to is-failable, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "failure of ".
    Done.

    /// What a failable kind holds when it is no failure.
    Bind text to failable-inner, given (the text kind):
        Return the characters from 12 to the end of kind.
    Done.

    Bind text to failable-c-name, given (the text kind):
        Define inner as cast failable-inner on (kind).
        If inner is "void", return "cfl_void".
        Return "cfl_{cast c-tag on (inner)}".
    Done.

    /// A failable's struct, and how one is made from a value, from a failure, or as done.
    Bind text to c-failable-helpers, given (the text kind):
        Define type-c as cast failable-c-name on (kind).
        Define inner as cast failable-inner on (kind).
        Define out as a chase.
        If inner is "void":
            Define c-language typedef-struct-cufetfailure-form, given (the term type-c),
                as [typedef struct { int ok; CufetFailure failure; } the type-c;].
            Insert "{typedef-struct-cufetfailure-form on (type-c)}\n" into out.
            Define c-language type-c-done-form, given (the term type-c, the term type-c-done),
                as [static the type-c the type-c-done(void) { the type-c o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); o.ok = 1; return o; }].
            Insert "{type-c-done-form on (type-c, "{type-c}_done")}\n" into out.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define c-language typedef-struct-type-form, given (the c-language axiom c-type, the term type-c),
                as [typedef struct { int ok; the c-type value; CufetFailure failure; } the type-c;].
            Insert "{typedef-struct-type-form on (cast c-type on (inner), type-c)}\n" into out.
            Define c-language type-c-some-form, given (the term type-c, the term type-c-some, the c-language axiom c-type),
                as [static the type-c the type-c-some(the c-type v) { the type-c o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); o.ok = 1; o.value = v; return o; }].
            Insert "{type-c-some-form on (type-c, "{type-c}_some", cast c-type on (inner))}\n" into out.
        Done.
        Define c-language type-c-fail-form, given (the term type-c, the term type-c-fail),
            as [static the type-c the type-c-fail(CufetFailure f) { the type-c o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); o.ok = 0; o.failure = f; return o; }].
        Insert "{type-c-fail-form on (type-c, "{type-c}_fail")}\n\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// Notes a failable type the program uses, after what it holds.
    Bind void to register-failable unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        If (the entry for kind in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for kind becomes true.
            Insert kind into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The kind of a written `<type> or failure`.
    Bind text or failure to failable-kind-of-type unto emitter, given (the node written):
        Define inner as "void".
        If (cast field-of on (written, 1))'s kind is not "VoidType":
            The inner becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If cast is-failable on (inner), return a failure (cast not-built on ("a failure of a {inner}")).
        Define kind as "failure of {inner}".
        Cast one's register-failable on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// A value going into a failable place: a failure as one, a value as a success.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-into-failable unto emitter, given (the c-language axiom value, the text source-kind, the text wanted):
        Define type-c as cast failable-c-name on (wanted).
        If source-kind is "failure", return call-of-one on ("{type-c}_fail", value).
        Return call-of-one on ("{type-c}_some", cast one's c-coerce on (value, source-kind, cast failable-inner on (wanted))).
    Done.

    /// The `Try` a statement is in — the label its failures go to — or "".
    Bind text to current-try unto emitter:
        Return the entry for "%try" in one's kinds but void is "".
    Done.

    /// The kind and C of an expression as it is, outside any `Try` — a failable left failable.
    Bind text or failure to raw-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kept as cast one's current-try.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes "".
        Define kind as cast one's kind-of on (expression) but on failure "".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes kept.
        If kind is "", return cast one's kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Return kind.
    Done.

    Bind c-language axiom or failure to raw-c-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kept as cast one's current-try.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes "".
        Define written as cast one's c-of on (expression) but on failure cast no-c.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes kept.
        If cast is-no-c on (written), return cast one's c-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Return written.
    Done.

    /// What every way out of a block undoes, in order.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-all-leaving, given (the c-language axiom unmakers, the c-language axiom frames, the c-language axiom rabbits, the c-language axiom files):
        Define c-language all-left, given (the c-language axiom unmakers, the c-language axiom frames, the c-language axiom rabbits, the c-language axiom files),
            as [the unmakers the frames the rabbits the files].
        Return all-left on (unmakers, frames, rabbits, files).
    Done.

    /// What a failable call's block ends on: its value, or nothing when it has none.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-unwrapped-value, given (the text kind):
        If cast failable-inner on (kind) is "void", return [(void)0].
        Return [cf_r.value].
    Done.

    /// A program's argv as C: its name, then each argument.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-spelled-out unto emitter, given (the c-language axiom program, the node handed):
        Define c-language one-more, given (the c-language axiom earlier, the c-language axiom argument), as [the earlier, (char*)(the argument)].
        Define spelled-out as program.
        For each argument in handed's children, repeat:
            The spelled-out becomes one-more on (spelled-out, cast one's c-of on (argument) or pass the failure off).
        Done.
        Return spelled-out.
    Done.

    /// What a call that can fail reads as here: inside a `Try`, its value.
    Bind text to unwrapped-kind unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-failable on (kind) and cast one's current-try is not "", return cast failable-inner on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// A call that can fail, as C: inside a `Try`, its value — or, when it fails, a jump to the handler.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-unwrapped unto emitter, given (the c-language axiom written, the text kind):
        Define label as cast one's current-try.
        If cast is-failable on (kind) is false or label is "", return written.
        Define c-language jumped, given (the term type-c, the c-language axiom written, the term failure-name, the c-language axiom leaving, the term handler, the c-language axiom value),
            as [({ the type-c cf_r = the written; if (!cf_r.ok) { the failure-name = cf_r.failure; the leaving goto the handler; } the value; })].
        Define leaving as cast c-all-leaving on (
            cast one's c-leaving-unmakers on (the entry for "%try-um" in one's kinds but void is ""),
            cast one's c-leaving on (the entry for "%try-exc" in one's kinds but void is "0"),
            cast one's c-leaving-rabbits on (the entry for "%try-rabbit" in one's kinds but void is "0"),
            cast one's c-leaving-files on (the entry for "%try-files" in one's kinds but void is "0")).
        Return jumped on (cast failable-c-name on (kind), written, "cf_failure_{label}", leaving, "cf_try_{label}", cast c-unwrapped-value on (kind)).
    Done.

    /// `<call> or pass the failure off` — its value, or the failure handed to this function's caller.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-pass-off unto emitter, given (the node held):
        Define kind as cast one's raw-kind-of on (held) or pass the failure off.
        Define written as cast one's raw-c-of on (held) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-failable on (kind) is false, return written.
        Define outer as the entry for "%return" in one's kinds but void is "".
        If cast is-failable on (outer) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("passing a failure off from where nothing can fail")).
        Define c-language passed-off, given (the term type-c, the c-language axiom written, the c-language axiom leaving, the term fail, the c-language axiom value),
            as [({ the type-c cf_r = the written; if (!cf_r.ok) { the leaving cufet_alloc_override = cf_fo; return the fail(cf_r.failure); } the value; })].
        Define leaving as cast c-all-leaving on (cast one's c-leaving-unmakers on ("0"), cast one's c-leaving on ("0"),
            cast one's c-leaving-rabbits on ("0"), cast one's c-leaving-files on ("0")).
        Return passed-off on (cast failable-c-name on (kind), written, leaving, "{cast failable-c-name on (outer)}_fail", cast c-unwrapped-value on (kind)).
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind fact to is-failure-expression, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "FailureLiteral" or kind is "FailurePropagate" or kind is "FailureFallback" or kind is "FileReadExpression"
            or kind is "DirectoryContentsExpression" or kind is "RunExpression" or kind is "PipeExpression".
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to failure-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "FailureLiteral", return "failure".
        If kind is "DirectoryContentsExpression":
            Cast one's register-failable on ("failure of series of text").
            Return cast one's unwrapped-kind on ("failure of series of text").
        Done.
        If kind is "RunExpression" or kind is "PipeExpression", return cast one's unwrapped-kind on (cast one's run-kind or pass the failure off).
        If kind is "FileReadExpression":
            Define read-kind as "failure of text".
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "AllLines", the read-kind becomes "failure of series of text".
            Otherwise if (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is not "All", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a file read of {(cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word}")).
            Cast one's register-failable on (read-kind).
            Return cast one's unwrapped-kind on (read-kind).
        Done.
        Define held as cast one's raw-kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-failable on (held) is false, return held.
        Return cast failable-inner on (held).
    Done.

    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-failure-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "FailureLiteral":
            Define said as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define tagged as c-verbatim on ([NULL]).
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) is false:
                The tagged becomes cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Define c-language failure-made, given (the c-language axiom said, the c-language axiom tagged), as [((CufetFailure){ the said, the tagged })].
            Return failure-made on (said, tagged).
        Done.
        If kind is "FileReadExpression":
            Define path-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Define read-c as cast no-c.
            Define read-kind as "failure of text".
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s word is "AllLines":
                The read-kind becomes "failure of series of text".
                Define c-language lines-read, given (the c-language axiom file-path),
                    as [({ cfl_cser_text cf_fr; memset(&cf_fr, 0, sizeof cf_fr); const char** cf_lp; int cf_ln; CufetFailure cf_fe; if (cufet_file_read_lines(the file-path, &cf_lp, &cf_ln, &cf_fe)) { cser_text* cf_ls = cser_text_new(); for (int cf_lj = 0; cf_lj < cf_ln; cf_lj++) cser_text_append(cf_ls, cf_lp[cf_lj]); cf_fr.ok = 1; cf_fr.value = cf_ls; } else cf_fr.failure = cf_fe; cf_fr; })].
                The read-c becomes lines-read on (path-c).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define c-language all-read, given (the c-language axiom file-path),
                    as [({ cfl_text cf_fr; memset(&cf_fr, 0, sizeof cf_fr); const char* cf_v; CufetFailure cf_fe; if (cufet_file_read_all(the file-path, &cf_v, &cf_fe)) { cf_fr.ok = 1; cf_fr.value = cf_v; } else cf_fr.failure = cf_fe; cf_fr; })].
                The read-c becomes all-read on (path-c).
            Done.
            Cast one's register-failable on (read-kind).
            Return cast one's c-unwrapped on (read-c, read-kind).
        Done.
        // `the contents of the directory <path>` — its entries' names, or a failure.
        If kind is "DirectoryContentsExpression":
            Define folder-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's register-failable on ("failure of series of text").
            Define c-language contents-read, given (the c-language axiom folder),
                as [({ cfl_cser_text cf_dc; memset(&cf_dc, 0, sizeof cf_dc); const char** cf_di; int cf_dn; CufetFailure cf_de; if (cufet_dir_contents(the folder, &cf_di, &cf_dn, &cf_de)) { cser_text* cf_ds = cser_text_new(); for (int cf_i = 0; cf_i < cf_dn; cf_i++) cser_text_append(cf_ds, cf_di[cf_i]); cf_dc.ok = 1; cf_dc.value = cf_ds; } else cf_dc.failure = cf_de; cf_dc; })].
            Return cast one's c-unwrapped on (contents-read on (folder-c), "failure of series of text").
        Done.
        If kind is "RunExpression":
            Define run-c as cast one's c-run on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's c-unwrapped on (run-c, cast one's run-kind or pass the failure off).
        Done.
        If kind is "PipeExpression":
            Define piped-c as cast one's c-run-pipe on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's c-unwrapped on (piped-c, cast one's run-kind or pass the failure off).
        Done.
        If kind is "FailurePropagate", return cast one's c-pass-off on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        // `<call> but on failure <default>` — the default worked out only when the call failed.
        Define held as cast one's raw-kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define written as cast one's raw-c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-failable on (held) is false, return written.
        Define inner as cast failable-inner on (held).
        Define fallback as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), inner) or pass the failure off.
        Define c-language or-fallback, given (the term type-c, the c-language axiom written, the c-language axiom fallback),
            as [({ the type-c cf_r = the written; cf_r.ok ? cf_r.value : (the fallback); })].
        Return or-fallback on (cast failable-c-name on (held), written, fallback).
    Done.

    /// `the message of`, `the category of` a failure.
    Bind text to failure-field-kind, given (the text field-name):
        If field-name is "message", return "text".
        If field-name is "category", return "voidable text".
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind c-language axiom to c-failure-field, given (the c-language axiom failure-c, the text field-name):
        If field-name is "message", return field-read on (failure-c, "message").
        Define c-language category-read, given (the c-language axiom failure-c),
            as [({ CufetFailure cf_f = the failure-c; cf_f.category ? cvo_text_some(cf_f.category) : cvo_text_none(); })].
        Return category-read on (failure-c).
    Done.

    // ── Running a program ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// What `run` gives: the record of what the program did, or a failure when it could not start.
    Bind text or failure to run-kind unto emitter:
        Define named as a map from text to text.
        In named, the entry for "errors" becomes "text".
        In named, the entry for "exit-code" becomes "number".
        In named, the entry for "output" becomes "text".
        Define record-kind as cast record-kind-of on (a series of text, named).
        Cast one's register-record on (record-kind).
        Cast one's register-failable on ("failure of {record-kind}").
        Return "failure of {record-kind}".
    Done.

    /// `run <program> with arguments …` as C — the runtime's own call, the one `cufet build` makes:
    /// the program's output and errors kept apart, or, `with the terminal`, its own.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-run unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as cast one's run-kind or pass the failure off.
        Define record-kind as cast failable-inner on (kind).
        Define record-c as cast record-c-name on (record-kind).
        Define type-c as cast failable-c-name on (kind).
        Define program-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        // The arguments: written out, or a series of them — with the program's name first, as argv has it.
        Define argv-c as cast no-c.
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)):
            Define spelled-out as cast one's c-spelled-out on ([(char*)cf_pg], cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Define c-language argv-written, given (the c-language axiom spelled-out), as [char* cf_av[] = { the spelled-out, (char*)0 };].
            The argv-c becomes argv-written on (spelled-out).
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Define c-language argv-from-series, given (the c-language axiom held-series),
                as [cser_text* cf_avs = the held-series; char** cf_av = (char**)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)(cf_avs->len + 2) * sizeof(char*)); cf_av[0] = (char*)cf_pg; for (int cf_ai = 0; cf_ai < cf_avs->len; cf_ai++) cf_av[cf_ai + 1] = (char*)cf_avs->data[cf_ai]; cf_av[cf_avs->len + 1] = (char*)0;].
            The argv-c becomes argv-from-series on (series-c).
        Done.
        // `with input ""` hands the program an end of input at once; none leaves it reading this one's.
        Define input-c as c-verbatim on ([NULL]).
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 7)) is false:
            The input-c becomes cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 7)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define c-language run-done, given (the term record-c, the term errors, the term exit-code, the term output),
            as [cf_run.ok = 1; cf_run.value = (the record-c){ .the errors = cf_se, .the exit-code = cufet_dec_from_ll(cf_ex), .the output = cf_so };].
        Define done-c as run-done on (record-c, cast c-name on ("errors"), cast c-name on ("exit-code"), cast c-name on ("output")).
        Define c-language captured, given (the c-language axiom input), as [cufet_run_capture(cf_pg, cf_av, the input, &cf_so, &cf_se, &cf_ex, &cf_e)].
        Define call-c as captured on (input-c).
        // `with the terminal`: the child has this program's own streams, so nothing comes back but its exit code.
        If (cast field-of on (expression, 6))'s word is "true":
            The call-c becomes c-verbatim on ([cufet_run_inherit(cf_pg, cf_av, &cf_e, &cf_ex)]).
            Define c-language nothing-kept, given (the c-language axiom finished), as [cf_so = ""; cf_se = ""; the finished].
            The done-c becomes nothing-kept on (done-c).
        Done.
        Define c-language program-run, given (the c-language axiom program, the c-language axiom argv, the term type-c, the c-language axiom call, the c-language axiom finished),
            as [({ const char* cf_pg = the program; the argv the type-c cf_run; memset(&cf_run, 0, sizeof cf_run); const char* cf_so = 0; const char* cf_se = 0; int cf_ex = 0; CufetFailure cf_e; if (the call) { the finished } else cf_run.failure = cf_e; cf_run; })].
        Return program-run on (program-c, argv-c, type-c, call-c, done-c).
    Done.

    /// The programs a pipe runs, left to right — `run "seq" | run "grep" | run "wc"`.
    Bind series of node or failure to piped-stages, given (the node expression):
        Define stages as a series of node.
        If expression's kind is "RunExpression":
            Insert expression into stages.
            Return stages.
        Done.
        If expression's kind is not "PipeExpression", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a pipe of a {expression's kind}")).
        For each stage in cast piped-stages on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off, insert stage into stages.
        For each stage in cast piped-stages on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off, insert stage into stages.
        Return stages.
    Done.

    /// One program of a pipe made ready to run: its name in `cf_pg<n>`, its argv in `cf_av<n>`.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-run-stage unto emitter, given (the node stage, the number place):
        If (cast field-of on (stage, 6))'s word is "true", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a pipe stage given the terminal")).
        Define program-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (stage, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (stage, 3)) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a pipe stage given its arguments as a series")).
        Define c-language program-named, given (the term program), as [(char*)the program].
        Define spelled-out as cast one's c-spelled-out on (program-named on ("cf_pg{place}"), cast field-of on (stage, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define c-language stage-ready, given (the term name, the c-language axiom program, the term argv, the c-language axiom spelled-out),
            as [const char* the name = the program; char* the argv[] = { the spelled-out, (char*)0 };].
        Return stage-ready on ("cf_pg{place}", program-c, "cf_av{place}", spelled-out).
    Done.

    /// `run … | run …` — each program run in turn, fed what the one before it wrote, as the
    /// interpreter runs them: the errors of all of them, the last non-zero exit, the last output.
    /// A program that cannot be started is the pipe's failure.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-run-pipe unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as cast one's run-kind or pass the failure off.
        Define record-c as cast record-c-name on (cast failable-inner on (kind)).
        Define type-c as cast failable-c-name on (kind).
        Define stages as cast piped-stages on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define prepared as cast no-c.
        Define first-input as c-verbatim on ([NULL]).
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (item 1 of stages, 7)) is false:
            The first-input becomes cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (item 1 of stages, 7)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define c-language stage-added, given (the c-language axiom earlier, the c-language axiom stage), as [the earlier the stage].
        Define c-language stage-chained, given (the c-language axiom earlier, the term program, the term argv),
            as [the earlier if (cf_ok) { if (cufet_run_capture(the program, the argv, cf_cur, &cf_so, &cf_se, &cf_ex, &cf_e)) { cf_eagg = cufet_str_concat(cf_eagg, cf_se); if (cf_ex != 0) cf_code = cf_ex; cf_cur = cf_so; } else { cf_run.failure = cf_e; cf_ok = 0; } }].
        Define chained as cast no-c.
        Define place as 0.
        For each stage in stages, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            The prepared becomes stage-added on (prepared, cast one's c-run-stage on (stage, place) or pass the failure off).
            The chained becomes stage-chained on (chained, "cf_pg{place}", "cf_av{place}").
        Done.
        Define c-language pipe-done, given (the term record-c, the term errors, the term exit-code, the term output),
            as [cf_run.ok = 1; cf_run.value = (the record-c){ .the errors = cf_eagg, .the exit-code = cufet_dec_from_ll(cf_code), .the output = cf_cur ? cf_cur : "" };].
        Define done-c as pipe-done on (record-c, cast c-name on ("errors"), cast c-name on ("exit-code"), cast c-name on ("output")).
        Define c-language pipe-run, given (the c-language axiom prepared, the term type-c, the c-language axiom first-input, the c-language axiom chained, the c-language axiom finished),
            as [({ the prepared the type-c cf_run; memset(&cf_run, 0, sizeof cf_run); const char* cf_so = 0; const char* cf_se = 0; int cf_ex = 0; CufetFailure cf_e; const char* cf_cur = the first-input; const char* cf_eagg = ""; int cf_code = 0; int cf_ok = 1; the chained if (cf_ok) { the finished } cf_run; })].
        Return pipe-run on (prepared, type-c, first-input, chained, done-c).
    Done.

    /// `run … | run ….` written as a statement — what the last program wrote goes to this program's
    /// output, and what they all said on their errors to its errors, as a shell has it.
    Bind void or failure to emit-run-pipe unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as cast one's run-kind or pass the failure off.
        Define piped-c as cast one's c-run-pipe on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Define record-kind as cast failable-inner on (kind).
        Define c-language run-shown, given (the term errors, the term output), as [fputs(cf_pr.value.the errors, stderr); fputs(cf_pr.value.the output, stdout);].
        Define shown as run-shown on (cast c-name on ("errors"), cast c-name on ("output")).
        If cast one's current-try is not "":
            Define c-language failable-name-piped-form, given (the term failable-c-name, the c-language axiom piped-c, the term current-try-cf-failure, the c-language axiom leaving, the term current-try-cf-try, the c-language axiom shown),
                as [{ the failable-c-name cf_pr = the piped-c; if (!cf_pr.ok) { the current-try-cf-failure = cf_pr.failure; the leaving goto the current-try-cf-try; } the shown }].
            Cast one's put on (failable-name-piped-form on (cast failable-c-name on (kind), piped-c, "cf_failure_{cast one's current-try}", cast c-all-leaving on (cast one's c-leaving-unmakers on (the entry for "%try-um" in one's kinds but void is ""), cast one's c-leaving on (the entry for "%try-exc" in one's kinds but void is "0"), cast one's c-leaving-rabbits on (the entry for "%try-rabbit" in one's kinds but void is "0"), cast one's c-leaving-files on (the entry for "%try-files" in one's kinds but void is "0")), "cf_try_{cast one's current-try}", shown)).
            Return.
        Done.
        Define c-language failable-name-piped-form-2, given (the term failable-c-name, the c-language axiom piped-c, the c-language axiom shown),
            as [{ the failable-c-name cf_pr = the piped-c; if (!cf_pr.ok) { fprintf(stderr, "%s\n", cf_pr.failure.message); exit(1); } the shown }].
        Cast one's put on (failable-name-piped-form-2 on (cast failable-c-name on (kind), piped-c, shown)).
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `Cast <call> or pass the failure off.`, or a call that can fail made inside a `Try`.
    Bind void or failure to emit-failable-cast unto emitter, given (the node call, the fact passes-off):
        If passes-off:
            Cast one's line on ("{cast one's c-pass-off on (call) or pass the failure off};").
            Return.
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("{cast one's c-of on (call) or pass the failure off};").
    Done.

    // ── Exceptions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// How many `Try`s with `In case of exception` are open around this statement, in this function.
    Bind number to exceptions-open unto emitter:
        Return (the entry for "%exc" in one's kinds but void is "0") converted to number but void is 0.
    Done.

    /// The C that closes the exception `Try`s a jump leaves — those opened since `depth` — or "".
    Bind c-language axiom to c-leaving unto emitter, given (the text depth):
        Define left as cast one's exceptions-open - (depth converted to number but void is 0).
        If left is less than 1, return [].
        Define c-language frames-dropped, given (the number left), as [cufet_exc_top -= the left; ].
        Return frames-dropped on (left).
    Done.

    /// A `Return`, closing every exception `Try` it leaves first — its value worked out before
    /// that, so a fault in it is still caught.
    Bind text to c-return unto emitter, given (the c-language axiom value):
        Define leaving as "{cast one's c-leaving-unmakers on ("0")}{cast one's c-leaving on ("0")}{cast one's c-leaving-rabbits on ("0")}{cast one's c-leaving-files on ("0")}cufet_alloc_override = cf_fo; ".
        If leaving is "":
            If cast is-no-c on (value), return "return;".
            Return "return {value};".
        Done.
        If cast is-no-c on (value), return "{cast c-open} {leaving}return; {cast c-close}".
        Define gives as the entry for "%return" in one's kinds but void is "".
        Return "{cast c-open} {cast c-type on (gives)} cf_ret = {value}; {leaving}return cf_ret; {cast c-close}".
    Done.

    /// `Stop` or `Skip` — closing the exception `Try`s opened inside the loop it leaves.
    Bind text to c-loop-jump unto emitter, given (the text jump):
        Define leaving as "{cast one's c-leaving-unmakers on (the entry for "%loop-um" in one's kinds but void is "")}{cast one's c-leaving on (the entry for "%loop-exc" in one's kinds but void is "0")}{cast one's c-leaving-rabbits on (the entry for "%loop-rabbit" in one's kinds but void is "0")}{cast one's c-leaving-files on (the entry for "%loop-files" in one's kinds but void is "0")}".
        If leaving is "", return "{jump};".
        Return "{cast c-open} {leaving}{jump}; {cast c-close}".
    Done.

    /// Marks the start of a loop's body, so a `Stop` in it knows what it leaves. Gives back what to put back.
    Bind text to entering-loop unto emitter:
        Define kept as "{the entry for "%loop-exc" in one's kinds but void is "0"}/{the entry for "%loop-rabbit" in one's kinds but void is "0"}/{the entry for "%loop-files" in one's kinds but void is "0"}/{the entry for "%loop-um" in one's kinds but void is "0"}".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-exc" becomes "{cast one's exceptions-open}".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-rabbit" becomes "{cast one's rabbits-open}".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-files" becomes "{cast one's files-open}".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-um" becomes cast one's next-block-depth.
        Return kept.
    Done.

    Bind void to leaving-loop unto emitter, given (the text kept):
        Define parts as kept split by "/".
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-exc" becomes item 1 of parts.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-rabbit" becomes item 2 of parts.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-files" becomes item 3 of parts.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%loop-um" becomes item 4 of parts.
    Done.

    /// The name a handler's exception is bound to: `the exception`, or the name it was given.
    Bind text to exception-binding, given (the node statement):
        Define named as "exception".
        For each place in range 1 to the number of statement's children, repeat:
            If (item place of statement's children)'s word is ":ExceptionName":
                The named becomes cast unquoted on (item (place + 1) of statement's children).
            Done.
        Done.
        If named is "exception", return "the exception".
        Return named.
    Done.

    /// `Try to: …` with `In case of failure:`, `In case of exception:`, or both. A failure inside goes
    /// to its handler, which sees it as `the failure`; an exception — a fault the checker cannot
    /// rule out — to the other, which sees it as `the exception` and RAISES IT AGAIN when it ends,
    /// unless it said `Suppress the exception.` Either way the program goes on after the `Try`.
    Bind void or failure to emit-try unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define failing as cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) is false.
        Define catching as cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) is false.
        Define label as "{(cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word}_{(cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word}".
        Define outer-try as cast one's current-try.
        Define outer-try-exc as the entry for "%try-exc" in one's kinds but void is "0".
        Define outer-try-rabbit as the entry for "%try-rabbit" in one's kinds but void is "0".
        Define outer-try-files as the entry for "%try-files" in one's kinds but void is "0".
        Define outer-try-um as the entry for "%try-um" in one's kinds but void is "0".
        Define outer-exc as "{cast one's exceptions-open}".
        // ★ When every handler leaves, what the body defines outlives it (`keeps-body-names`), so the
        // `Try` opens no C block of its own: the body's variables are the enclosing block's.
        Define keeps as cast checker's keeps-body-names on (statement).
        Define outer as one's indent.
        If keeps is false:
            Cast one's put on ([{]).
            The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("CufetFailure cf_failure_{label}; memset(&cf_failure_{label}, 0, sizeof cf_failure_{label}); int cf_tov_{label} = cufet_alloc_override; (void)cf_tov_{label};").
        If catching:
            // Taken before the jump point and never changed after it, so they hold their values
            // across the jump back.
            Cast one's line on ("int cf_xf_{label} = cufet_nfiles; int cf_xa_{label} = cufet_arena_top; int cf_sup_{label} = 0; const char* cf_xmsg_{label} = 0; (void)cf_sup_{label}; (void)cf_xmsg_{label};").
            Cast one's line on ("if (CUFET_PLAIN_SETJMP(cufet_exc_bufs[++cufet_exc_top]) != 0) goto cf_catch_{label};").
            Cast one's line on ("cufet_exc_um[cufet_exc_top] = cufet_num; cufet_exc_arena[cufet_exc_top] = cf_xa_{label};").
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%exc" becomes "{cast one's exceptions-open + 1}".
        Done.
        If keeps is false, cast one's put on ([{]).
        If failing:
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes label.
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-exc" becomes outer-exc.
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-rabbit" becomes "{cast one's rabbits-open}".
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-files" becomes "{cast one's files-open}".
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-um" becomes cast one's next-block-depth.
        Done.
        If keeps:
            Cast one's emit-kept-body on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try" becomes outer-try.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-exc" becomes outer-try-exc.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-rabbit" becomes outer-try-rabbit.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-files" becomes outer-try-files.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%try-um" becomes outer-try-um.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%exc" becomes outer-exc.
        If keeps is false, cast one's put on ([}]).
        If catching, cast one's line on ("cufet_exc_top--;").
        Cast one's line on ("goto cf_tried_{label};").
        // A failure arrives with this `Try`'s own frame already closed, by the jump that brought it.
        If failing:
            Define c-language label-try-cufet-form, given (the term label-cf-try, the term label-cf-tov),
                as [the label-cf-try: { cufet_alloc_override = the label-cf-tov;].
            Cast one's put on (label-try-cufet-form on ("cf_try_{label}", "cf_tov_{label}")).
            Define kept as cast one's kinds-kept.
            In one's kinds, the entry for "the failure" becomes "failure".
            Cast one's declared-here on ("the failure").
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%the failure" becomes "failure".
            In one's kinds, the entry for "@the failure" becomes "".
            The one's indent becomes outer joined to "        ".
            Cast one's line on ("CufetFailure {cast c-name on ("the failure")} = cf_failure_{label};").
            Define failure-begun as cast one's opening-scope.
            For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children, repeat:
                Cast one's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Cast one's closing-scope on (failure-begun).
            The one's kinds becomes kept.
            The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
            Cast one's put on ([}]).
            Cast one's line on ("goto cf_tried_{label};").
        Done.
        If catching:
            // What the jump passed over: files opened and regions entered since the `Try` began.
            Cast one's line on ("cf_catch_{label}: cufet_exc_top--; cf_xmsg_{label} = cufet_exc_msg; cufet_close_files_from(cf_xf_{label}); while (cufet_arena_top > cf_xa_{label}) cufet_arena_merge_down(); cufet_alloc_override = cf_tov_{label};").
            Cast one's put on ([{]).
            Define kept as cast one's kinds-kept.
            Define bound as cast exception-binding on (statement).
            In one's kinds, the entry for bound becomes "exception".
            Cast one's declared-here on (bound).
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%{bound}" becomes "exception".
            In one's kinds, the entry for "@{bound}" becomes "".
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%suppress" becomes label.
            The one's indent becomes outer joined to "        ".
            Cast one's line on ("const char* {cast c-name on (bound)} = cf_xmsg_{label};").
            Define exception-begun as cast one's opening-scope.
            For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Cast one's emit-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Cast one's closing-scope on (exception-begun).
            The one's kinds becomes kept.
            The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
            Cast one's put on ([}]).
            Cast one's line on ("cf_done_{label}: ;").
            Cast one's line on ("if (!cf_sup_{label}) cufet_raise(cf_xmsg_{label});").
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("cf_tried_{label}: ;").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        If keeps is false, cast one's put on ([}]).
    Done.

    /// A kept `Try` body, written where it stands: its names stay known after it, and what it makes is
    /// registered to be unmade — so a failure part-way unmakes it — and then handed on, as
    /// `Interpreter.ExitScopeIntoEnclosing` hands it: to an enclosing block, which unmakes it at its end,
    /// or to a frame or the top level, which unmakes nothing, so it is dropped unrun.
    Bind void or failure to emit-kept-body unto emitter, given (the node statements):
        Define was-in-block as the entry for "%in-block" in one's kinds but void is "".
        Define blocks-before as the entry for "%blocks" in one's kinds but void is "0".
        Define begun as cast one's opening-scope.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Cast one's emit-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If begun is not "" and was-in-block is not "yes", cast one's line on ("cufet_num = {begun};").
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%in-block" becomes was-in-block.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%blocks" becomes blocks-before.
    Done.

    /// `Write <text> to the file <path>.` and `Append …` — inside a `Try`, a failure goes to its
    /// handler; outside one it has nowhere to go, and the program says why and stops, as `cufet build`'s does.
    Bind void or failure to emit-file-write unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define appending as (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s word is "true".
        Define written-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define path-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's register-failable on ("failure of void").
        Define c-language file-written, given (the c-language axiom file-path, the c-language axiom written, the fact appending),
            as [({ cfl_void cf_w; memset(&cf_w, 0, sizeof cf_w); CufetFailure cf_we; if (cufet_file_write(the file-path, the written, the appending, &cf_we)) cf_w.ok = 1; else cf_w.failure = cf_we; cf_w; })].
        Define write-c as file-written on (path-c, written-c, appending).
        If cast one's current-try is not "":
            Cast one's line on ("{cast one's c-unwrapped on (write-c, "failure of void")};").
            Return.
        Done.
        Define c-language cfl-write-fpr-form, given (the c-language axiom write-c),
            as [{ cfl_void cf_w = the write-c; if (!cf_w.ok) { fprintf(stderr, "%s\n", cf_w.failure.message); exit(1); } }].
        Cast one's put on (cfl-write-fpr-form on (write-c)).
    Done.

    /// What a function that can only fail or be done says when it reaches its end: done.
    Bind void to close-failable unto emitter:
        If (the entry for "%return" in one's kinds but void is "") is "failure of void":
            Cast one's line on ("return cfl_void_done();").
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
